  {
   "title": "An accidental AI company",
   "energy": 0.6,
   "shots": [
    {
     "narration": "The story begins in nineteen ninety-three, in a booth at a Denny's diner near San Jose.",
     "scene": "backdrop",
     "params": {
      "style": "wave"
     },
     "camera": {
      "from": "wide",
      "to": "low"
     },
     "transition": "dip",
     "overlays": [
      {
       "type": "chapter",
       "index": 1,
       "title": "An Accidental AI Company",
       "at": 0.2
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "narration": "Three engineers, Jensen Huang, Chris Malachowsky and Curtis Priem, had a simple idea: build chips that make video games look better.",
     "scene": "timeline",
     "params": {
      "events": [
       {
        "year": "1993",
        "title": "NVIDIA founded"
       },
       {
        "year": "1999",
        "title": "GeForce 256",
        "sub": "Marketed as the first GPU"
       },
       {
        "year": "2006",
        "title": "CUDA released"
       },
       {
        "year": "2012",
        "title": "AlexNet"
       },
       {
        "year": "2016",
        "title": "First AI supercomputer",
        "sub": "Delivered to OpenAI"
       },
       {
        "year": "2022",
        "title": "ChatGPT launches"
       }
      ],
      "active": 0
     },
     "camera": {
      "from": "along",
      "to": "at0"
     },
     "overlays": [
      {
       "type": "lower",
       "text": "Three founders",
       "sub": "Huang · Malachowsky · Priem",
       "at": "@Jensen"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "narration": "In nineteen ninety-nine, they released the GeForce two fifty-six, and marketed it as the world's first graphics processing unit. The GPU.",
     "scene": "timeline",
     "continues": true,
     "params": {
      "active": 1
     },
     "camera": {
      "from": "at0",
      "to": "at1"
     }
    },
    {
     "narration": "For years, that was the whole business. Gamers bought graphics cards, and NVIDIA kept making them faster.",
     "scene": "gpu_card",
     "params": {
      "fans": 3,
      "label": "GRAPHICS CARD"
     },
     "camera": {
      "from": "wide",
      "to": "close",
      "orbit": 20
     }
    },
    {
     "narration": "Then, in two thousand six, the company made a strange and expensive bet. It released a software platform called CUDA.",
     "say": "Then, in two thousand six, the company made a strange and expensive bet. It released a software platform called Kooda.",
     "scene": "timeline",
     "params": {
      "events": [
       {
        "year": "1993",
        "title": "NVIDIA founded"
       },
       {
        "year": "1999",
        "title": "GeForce 256"
       },
       {
        "year": "2006",
        "title": "CUDA released",
        "sub": "GPUs for any heavy computation"
       },
       {
        "year": "2012",
        "title": "AlexNet"
       },
       {
        "year": "2016",
        "title": "First AI supercomputer",
        "sub": "Delivered to OpenAI"
       },
       {
        "year": "2022",
        "title": "ChatGPT launches"
       }
      ],
      "active": 2,
      "activeFrom": 1
     },
     "camera": {
      "from": "at1",
      "to": "at2"
     }
    },
    {
     "narration": "CUDA let scientists use a graphics card for something other than graphics. Any heavy calculation could now run on a GPU.",
     "say": "Kooda let scientists use a graphics card for something other than graphics. Any heavy calculation could now run on a G P U.",
     "scene": "gpu_card",
     "params": {
      "fans": 3,
      "explode": true
     },
     "camera": {
      "from": "side",
      "to": "chip"
     },
     "overlays": [
      {
       "type": "callout",
       "anchor": "chip",
       "text": "The GPU chip",
       "sub": "now a general-purpose engine",
       "at": "@heavy"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "narration": "Investors were skeptical. It was expensive, and for years, few customers were asking for it.",
     "scene": "chip",
     "params": {
      "label": "CUDA",
      "cores": 12,
      "activity": 0.12
     },
     "camera": {
      "from": "low",
      "to": "side"
     },
     "overlays": [
      {
       "type": "tag",
       "text": "2006 – 2011",
       "at": 0.4
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "narration": "But in twenty twelve, three researchers in Toronto used two NVIDIA gaming cards to train a neural network called AlexNet.",
     "scene": "timeline",
     "continues": false,
     "params": {
      "events": [
       {
        "year": "1993",
        "title": "NVIDIA founded"
       },
       {
        "year": "1999",
