  {
   "title": "Why a graphics chip?",
   "energy": 0.65,
   "shots": [
    {
     "narration": "So why did a chip built for video games turn out to be perfect for artificial intelligence?",
     "scene": "backdrop",
     "params": {
      "style": "galaxy"
     },
     "camera": {
      "from": "wide",
      "to": "hero"
     },
     "transition": "dip",
     "overlays": [
      {
       "type": "chapter",
       "index": 2,
       "title": "Why a Graphics Chip?",
       "at": 0.2
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "narration": "A traditional processor, a CPU, has a handful of powerful cores. It works through a job one step at a time.",
     "scene": "cores_compare",
     "params": {
      "leftLabel": "CPU",
      "rightLabel": "GPU",
      "leftCores": 8,
      "rightGrid": 32,
      "mode": "left"
     },
     "cues": {
      "left": "@works",
      "right": 30
     },
     "camera": {
      "from": "wide",
      "to": "left"
     }
    },
    {
     "narration": "Think of it as a brilliant chef who insists on cooking every dish alone.",
     "scene": "cores_compare",
     "continues": true,
     "params": {
      "mode": "left"
     },
     "camera": {
      "from": "left_cores",
      "to": "left"
     }
    },
    {
     "narration": "A GPU is different. It has thousands of smaller cores that all work at the same moment.",
     "scene": "cores_compare",
     "params": {
      "leftLabel": "CPU",
      "rightLabel": "GPU",
      "leftCores": 8,
      "rightGrid": 32,
      "mode": "right"
     },
     "cues": {
      "left": 0.1,
      "right": "@thousands"
     },
     "camera": {
      "from": "right",
      "to": "right_cores"
     },
     "transition": "fade"
    },
    {
     "narration": "It is a kitchen with a thousand cooks, each doing one small task, all at once.",
     "scene": "cores_compare",
     "continues": true,
     "params": {
      "mode": "right"
     },
     "camera": {
      "from": "right_cores",
      "to": "top"
     }
    },
    {
     "narration": "Give both the same job, and the GPU is finished while the CPU has barely started.",
     "scene": "cores_compare",
     "params": {
      "leftLabel": "CPU",
      "rightLabel": "GPU",
      "leftCores": 8,
      "rightGrid": 32,
      "mode": "both"
     },
     "cues": {
      "start": 0.3
     },
     "camera": {
      "from": "wide",
      "to": "angle"
     },
     "transition": "fade"
    },
    {
     "narration": "And a neural network is exactly that kind of job: millions of simple calculations that can all happen in parallel.",
     "scene": "neural_network",
     "params": {
      "layers": [
       6,
       9,
       9,
       9,
       4
      ],
      "activity": 0.95,
      "speed": 1.2
     },
     "camera": {
      "from": "side",
      "to": "front"
     }
    },
    {
     "narration": "Training a model means showing it data, measuring how wrong it is, and nudging billions of numbers to be slightly less wrong.",
     "scene": "loss_landscape",
     "params": {
      "seed": 4,
      "label": "How wrong the model is",
      "progress": 0.5
     },
     "camera": {
      "from": "wide",
      "to": "follow"
     }
    },
    {
     "narration": "Repeat that trillions of times, and you get a model that can write, draw and reason.",
     "scene": "loss_landscape",
     "continues": true,
     "params": {
      "seed": 4,
      "label": "How wrong the model is",
      "progress": 1
     },
     "camera": {
      "from": "follow",
      "to": "valley"
     }
    },
    {
     "narration": "Using the finished model is called inference. Every question you type triggers billions more calculations, on the same kind of chips.",
     "scene": "token_stream",
     "params": {
      "input": [
       "How",
       "do",
       "GPUs",
       "work",
       "?"
      ],
      "output": [
       "In",
       "parallel",
       "."
      ],
      "layers": 6
     },
     "cues": {
      "emit": "@triggers"
     },
     "camera": {
      "from": "input",
      "to": "wide"
     },
     "overlays": [
      {
       "type": "tag",
       "text": "Inference",
       "at": "@inference"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "narration": "On ordinary processors, training a frontier model would be impractically slow. On thousands of GPUs working together, it takes weeks.",
     "scene": "chip",
     "params": {
      "label": "GPU",
      "cores": 18,
      "explode": true
     },
     "camera": {
      "from": "top",
      "to": "die"
     },
     "overlays": [
      {
       "type": "callout",
       "anchor": "die",
       "text": "Thousands of parallel cores",
       "at": "@thousands"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
